From 0672ffbecde37c4bee957d07b82180f1d62cc253 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yann Gautier <yann.gautier@st.com>
Date: Wed, 6 May 2026 16:08:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 501/572] fix(st): cast the read_cntfrq_el0() return to
 unsigned int

The function plat_get_syscnt_freq2() returns an unsigned int type, but
read_cntfrq_el0() that is used inside will return an uint64_t value
on aarch64 platforms (STM32MP2). But this value is usually 64MHz (HSI)
or 24MHz (HSE). It will never be above 4GHz, so it is safe to cast its
return value.
The issue was found with clang -Wshorten-64-to-32 warning.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/arm-trusted-firmware.git 49fd8748650afc49dd3ef208d364464b8770240d fix(st): cast the read_cntfrq_el0() return to unsigned int]
Change-Id: Iab2162701cabfde4a4416bd4cea45eb15dbeeb5d
Signed-off-by: Yann Gautier <yann.gautier@st.com>
Reviewed-on: https://gerrit.st.com/c/mpu/oe/st/tf-a/+/572141
Domain-Review: Yann GAUTIER <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Maxime MERE <maxime.mere@foss.st.com>
Tested-by: Yann GAUTIER <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
Reviewed-by: Yann GAUTIER <yann.gautier@foss.st.com>
---
 plat/st/common/stm32mp_common.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/plat/st/common/stm32mp_common.c b/plat/st/common/stm32mp_common.c
index 433d86b15b..2b58b6cfb0 100644
--- a/plat/st/common/stm32mp_common.c
+++ b/plat/st/common/stm32mp_common.c
@@ -75,7 +75,14 @@ uintptr_t plat_get_ns_image_entrypoint(void)
 
 unsigned int plat_get_syscnt_freq2(void)
 {
-	return read_cntfrq_el0();
+	/*
+	 * The system counter clock will never be above 4GHz, it is usually set
+	 * at 64MHz (HSI) at startup, and then moved to another clock with a
+	 * lower frequency and more stable.
+	 * It is then safe to cast the return of read_cntfrq_el0 to a 32 bit
+	 * value to match the plat_get_syscnt_freq2 function prototype.
+	 */
+	return (unsigned int)read_cntfrq_el0();
 }
 
 static uintptr_t boot_ctx_address;
